{
  "explain": "The user asked two distinct questions. First, to find the total number of distinct campaign_ad_id and total conversions for Brand_ID = 'Dove' in Q1 2025 from the `campaign_performance_metrics_20Aug` table. I generated a SQL query to select the count of distinct `campaign_ad_id` and the sum of `conversions`, filtering by `brand_id` 'BRAND_013' (which corresponds to 'Dove') and dates within Q1 2025 (January 1, 2025, to March 31, 2025). Second, the user asked to list the top 5 selling products (sku_desc) by total units_sold in Q1 2025 from the `transaction_data` table. I generated a SQL query to select `sku_desc` and the sum of `unit_sold`, filtering by `transaction_date` within Q1 2025, grouping by `sku_desc`, ordering by `total_units_sold` in descending order, and limiting to the top 5 results. Both queries were validated and executed successfully.",
  "sql": "SELECT\n    COUNT(DISTINCT t1.campaign_ad_id) AS distinct_campaign_ad_id_count,\n    SUM(t1.conversions) AS total_conversions\n  FROM\n    `acn-cda.RMN_Campaign_Data_AgentTest.campaign_performance_metrics_20Aug` AS t1\n  WHERE\n    t1.brand_id = 'BRAND_013'\n    AND t1.date >= '2025-01-01'\n    AND t1.date < '2025-04-01';\n\nSELECT\n    t.sku_desc,\n    SUM(t.unit_sold) AS total_units_sold\n  FROM\n    `acn-cda.RMN_Campaign_Data_AgentTest.transaction_data` AS t\n  WHERE\n    t.transaction_date BETWEEN '2025-01-01' AND '2025-03-31'\n  GROUP BY\n    t.sku_desc\nORDER BY\n  total_units_sold DESC\nLIMIT 5;",
